10. Predict the Output – Matrix Processing
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
int main() {
int a[2][2] = {{1, 2}, {3, 4}};
int sum = 0;
for(int i = 0; i &lt; 2; i++)
for(int j = 0; j &lt; 2; j++)
sum += a[i][j];
printf(&quot;%d&quot;, sum);
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and determine the time complexity.
Matrix:
1 2
3 4
The nested loops add every element:
sum = 1 + 2 + 3 + 4
    = 10
Output:
10
Time complexity:
There are two nested loops:
for(i = 0; i < 2; i++)
    for(j = 0; j < 2; j++)
For a general n × n matrix:
O(n²)
